---
source: crates/sshpick-cli/src/cli/test.rs
expression: text
---
$ sshpick --lst
Error: unknown option "--lst"
Fix: sshpick accepts --help, --no-color, --non-interactive, --version. Did you mean --list?

$ sshpick list --lsit
Error: unknown option "--lsit"
Fix: sshpick list accepts --help, --json, --no-color, --non-interactive, --version. Did you mean --list?

$ sshpick --bogus
Error: unknown option "--bogus"
Fix: sshpick accepts --help, --no-color, --non-interactive, --version.

$ sshpick help lst
Error: unknown command "lst"
Fix: did you mean `sshpick help list`? See all commands with `sshpick --help`.

$ sshpick help bogus
Error: unknown command "bogus"
Fix: see all commands with `sshpick --help`.

$ sshpick consul < /dev/null
Error: 4 hosts match "consul", and the picker needs an interactive terminal
Fix: narrow the query to one host, or list them with `sshpick ls consul`.

$ TERM=dumb sshpick consul
Error: 4 hosts match "consul", and the picker needs a terminal that moves the cursor (TERM=dumb)
Fix: narrow the query to one host, or list them with `sshpick ls consul`.

$ sshpick --non-interactive
Error: 12 hosts to choose from, and --non-interactive never opens the picker
Fix: narrow the query to one host, or list them with `sshpick ls`.

$ sshpick lst new < /dev/null
Error: no host matches "lst new"
Fix: did you mean `sshpick list new`?

$ sshpick nope < /dev/null
Error: no host matches "nope"
Fix: list every host with `sshpick ls`.

$ sshpick inspekt stg-consul1 < /dev/null
Error: no host matches "inspekt stg-consul1"
Fix: did you mean `sshpick inspect stg-consul1`?

$ sshpick inspect
Error: sshpick inspect needs a query
Fix: name a host, as in `sshpick inspect stg-consul1`, or list them with `sshpick ls`.

$ sshpick inspect consul
Error: 3 hosts match "consul"; inspect needs exactly one
Fix: name one of stg-consul1, stg-consul2, stg-consul3, or list them with `sshpick ls consul`.

$ sshpick inspect web
Error: 8 hosts match "web"; inspect needs exactly one
Fix: name one of web1, web2, web3, web4, web5 and 3 more, or list them with `sshpick ls web`.

$ sshpick inspect stg-broken
Error: /home/me/.ssh/config: terminating, 1 bad configuration options

$ sshpick inspect stg-slow
Error: ssh -G gave no answer within 2 s

$ sshpick  # no Host lines
Error: no hosts found in ~/.ssh/config or the files it Includes
Fix: add `Host` lines; ENV and WHAT come from comments.
Learn More: https://github.com/PunGrumpy/sshpick/blob/main/docs/configuration.md#config-conventions

$ sshpick  # no ~/.ssh/config
Error: cannot read /nonexistent-home/.ssh/config: No such file or directory (os error 2)

$ sshpick  # no HOME
Error: cannot find the home directory

$ sshpick stg-consul1  # no ssh
Error: cannot run ssh: No such file or directory (os error 2)
Fix: install OpenSSH, or put `ssh` on your PATH.

$ sshpick stg-consul1  # ssh refused
Error: cannot run ssh: Permission denied (os error 13)

$ sshpick ls  # stdout is full
Error: cannot write the host list: No space left on device (os error 28)
